rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: quality
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must be expressed using a structured YAML decision schema
    rather than unstructured narrative text to enable machine processing and consistent
    interpretation.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in decision records
    (ADR); all other representations, including pattern metadata and AEM, must be
    derived from ADR.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created with a supporting classification by default
    to ensure they are validated through evidence before becoming foundational core
    patterns.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers to preserve clarity between governance, execution, contracts, and reliability.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the system-wide hierarchy for conflict resolution: Global Rules
    take absolute precedence over Project Rules, which take precedence over Prompt
    Rules.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability and grounding in observed behavior.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle) without conflating the two dimensions.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that candidate signals satisfy recurrence, system impact, reusability,
    and stability criteria before being promoted to patterns.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts (AEM, AID) must summarize authoritative
    sources and must not store manually introduced state that should reside in durable
    source artifacts.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces separation of concerns where CAS Runner orchestrates and workflows
    reason, preventing workflows from performing direct repository discovery or knowledge
    scanning.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item must be derived from its decision
    status; items not marked as 'accepted' cannot be classified as 'DONE'.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from recreating global, runtime, or template governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for planning state; all generated
    artifacts must derive planning status from the Architecture Work Registry.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must remain consistent with and never
    contradict existing Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring all system-proposed architectural
    decisions to be explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR files before
    they can be reflected in the AEM or other system artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are restricted to foundational architectural primitives and
    must not include context-specific strategies or implementation details.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to the core classification requires strong evidence,
    preferably originating from multiple sources or system contexts.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational global rule defining the semantic contract for language in
    artifacts, specifically distinguishing between intent, decisions, and system state.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
